+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+## This Voyage
+
+TodoMVC app, vanilla JavaScript, localStorage persistence. Six feature files, 41 scenarios total.
+
+### Specs authored
+
+- `features/new-todo.feature` -- 7 scenarios: creation, trim, empty guard, visibility
+- `features/todo-item.feature` -- 11 scenarios: toggle, double-click edit, save/discard, destroy
+- `features/toggle-all.feature` -- 7 scenarios: mark all, clear completed, checkbox sync
+- `features/counter.feature` -- 5 scenarios: active count, pluralization
+- `features/routing.feature` -- 4 scenarios: #/, #/active, #/completed, default
+- `features/persistence.feature` -- 4 scenarios: reload survival for todos, completed, deleted, edited
+
+### Decisions
+
+- Single `js/app.js` for all production code per spec's recommended structure.
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanilla` (framework identifier is "vanilla").
+- Routing via hashchange listener, no external library.
+- Template HTML cleaned of comments, adapted from `assets/app-template.index.html`.
+
+### Open questions
+
+- None at spec time.
diff --git a/features/counter.feature b/features/counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3c6e3ae
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many todos are left
+  So that I know my remaining workload
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero items when no todos exist
+    Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows singular form for one active todo
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows plural form for multiple active todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter excludes completed todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero when all todos are completed
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "0 items left"
diff --git a/features/new-todo.feature b/features/new-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d998221
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/new-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+Feature: New todo creation
+  As a user
+  I want to add new todos
+  So that I can track tasks I need to complete
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Page loads with empty state
+    Then the new todo input is visible
+    And the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: New todo is added on Enter
+    When the user types "Buy milk" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+    And the todo at position 1 is not completed
+    And the new todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: Input is trimmed before creating
+    When the user types "  Buy milk  " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Empty input does not create a todo
+    When the user presses Enter in the new todo input
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only input does not create a todo
+    When the user types "   " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Multiple todos can be added
+    When the user types "Buy milk" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+    And the todo at position 2 has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer appear after adding a todo
+    When the user types "Buy milk" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d134afc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist across page reload
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+    And the todo at position 2 has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Completed state persists across page reload
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has completed the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+  Scenario: Deleted todos stay deleted across page reload
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user hovers over the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user clicks the destroy button for todo "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the todo at position 1 has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Edited titles persist across page reload
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy eggs" in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user presses Enter in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy eggs"
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..65ca5e4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+Feature: Route-based filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter todos by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: All route shows all todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user has completed the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is visible in the list
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible in the list
+    And the "All" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user has completed the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible in the list
+    And the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user has completed the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is visible in the list
+    And the "Completed" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Default route is all
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the "All" filter link is selected
diff --git a/features/todo-item.feature b/features/todo-item.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..71ceb16
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-item.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+Feature: Todo item interactions
+  As a user
+  I want to manage individual todo items
+  So that I can track completion and edit titles
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+    And the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox marks a todo as complete
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    And the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox again marks a todo as active
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a label activates editing mode
+    When the user double-clicks the label for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    And the edit input for todo "Buy milk" contains "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Editing is saved on Enter
+    When the user double-clicks the label for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy eggs" in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user presses Enter in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy eggs"
+    And the todo "Buy eggs" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Editing is saved on blur
+    When the user double-clicks the label for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy eggs" in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user blurs the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy eggs"
+
+  Scenario: Editing is discarded on Escape
+    When the user double-clicks the label for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy eggs" in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user presses Escape in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    When the user double-clicks the label for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user clears the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user presses Enter in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Editing input is trimmed
+    When the user double-clicks the label for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "  Buy eggs  " in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user presses Enter in the edit input for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy eggs"
+
+  Scenario: Destroy button removes a todo
+    When the user hovers over the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user clicks the destroy button for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Completed todo shows checked checkbox
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk" is checked
+
+  Scenario: Active todo shows unchecked checkbox
+    Then the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk" is not checked
diff --git a/features/toggle-all.feature b/features/toggle-all.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a216141
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-all.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+Feature: Mark all as complete
+  As a user
+  I want to mark all todos as complete at once
+  So that I can quickly finish all my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all marks all todos as complete
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all marks all todos as active
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    And the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not completed
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is not completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all checks when all todos are individually completed
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all unchecks when a todo is unchecked
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes completed todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user clicks the clear-completed button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the todo at position 1 has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when completed todos exist
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the clear-completed button is visible
